{"artifacts":[],"checksum":"sha256:caf59563475bb0f1204d941902089c6a923aa1d2faaff379aa931bcd5242c9cc","events":[{"actor":{"id":"system-runtime","type":"system"},"artifactRefs":[],"eventHash":"sha256:239690ca4129ca12c240967f4252267ccce70e11e92a44b6940fcb7cd186d8d7","eventId":"event-7084b334-699d-40a6-8dc6-fec78726fd68","evidenceRefs":[{"ciphertextSha256":"32208ae070dc910f163622e4da3ad1970134f05b1c363a952cc5b5a3c99f2f47","contentSha256":"2eef4190e3522ef5be58dc7dfdcc4611b9a7d02d7ccda35ce25d93f93f143f81","evidenceId":"exec-exec-m08-judge9-judge-a1-judgment"}],"idempotencyKey":"node-outcome-727dab99-2b0c-4087-a3db-becca3480666","kind":{"data":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge9","nextState":"failed","nodeId":"judge","outcome":"terminal_failure","reason":"judge_refused"},"type":"node_outcome_recorded"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-19T01:37:27.597969400Z","previousHash":"sha256:27b839bc6e97c4a544fd5297629d73edb847b18be5da83179525318822660880","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge9","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":18,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge9"},{"actor":{"id":"system-runtime","type":"system"},"artifactRefs":[],"eventHash":"sha256:96b5ec4266a10b4cb3e22874be57cf4c2b0d8b3c1947adcfcf29030c68389c12","eventId":"event-d9e193ec-9667-4918-8a17-614fe1ddb09d","evidenceRefs":[],"idempotencyKey":"gate-verdict-8896c99b-b6e0-4b63-a226-47ea5c05eb73","kind":{"data":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge9","findings":[{"claim":"The one-glance verdict defaults to attention=\"unknown\" for any node without a pre-declared silence budget. On first open of exec-m08-judge9 the monitor answered \"unknown\" with reason silence_unevaluated/no_declared_budget, and it stayed \"unknown\" through 101s of node silence. The operator's core question (sleep or not?) has no answer until they hand-configure a per-node bound, which is exactly the work the monitor exists to avoid.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Ship a default execution-level silence bound (or derive one from observed node runtimes) so attention resolves to ok/needs_you on first read; reserve \"unknown\" for genuinely unobservable state and never for missing config that the runtime could default.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"amend_budget's freshness token is not what its schema says. Passing the exact computed_at_sequence the verdict published (14) was refused: \"computed against sequence 14, and the execution has moved to 0\". Only computedAtSequence=0 was accepted; the next call then demanded 15. The field tracks the last accepted amendment, not the verdict frontier, so the documented remedy path fails on first use.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Either make amend_budget accept the verdict's own computed_at_sequence (as documented and as the remedy payload advertises), or rename the field and return the expected value in the verdict itself so the operator can act without a guess-and-retry loop.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"A node that failed and requeued is invisible in the glance. flaky_check recorded retryable_failure (tool_exited_non_zero) at seq 11 and has sat in `queued` for over 2 minutes; status shows failed:0, queued:1 and lists no attentionReason for it — even after a 30s silence budget was explicitly declared for that node. Silence appears to be evaluated only for `running` nodes, so a run wedged in queue reads as healthy forever.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Evaluate silence budgets for queued/waiting nodes too, and surface retry churn in the glance (e.g. a retrying/degraded count or a retry_exhaustion attention reason) instead of folding failed-and-requeued back into a benign `queued` tally.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"attention=\"needs_you\" carries no remedy or urgency. The reason object is bare {\"kind\":\"silent_node\",\"node\":\"judge\"} — unlike the silence_unevaluated reason, which did carry an operation and remedy. The operator learns they cannot sleep but not what to do or how bad it is.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Attach the same remedy/operation shape (and a severity or since-timestamp) to every actionable attention reason, including silent_node.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"acceptedMutations stays 0 after mutations are accepted. Two amend_budget calls succeeded and moved headSequence 14 -> 15 -> 17, yet every subsequent status still reports acceptedMutations:0. An operator using that counter to confirm their intervention landed gets a false negative.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Increment acceptedMutations on every accepted mutation, or drop the field if it means something narrower than its name suggests and document that meaning.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"Arming the wake lease appends to the same sequence space as real work: wake_arm returned headSequence 14 with contentHead 13, so a monitoring action inflates the head the operator uses to judge progress and to build the amend_budget token.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Keep lease bookkeeping off the content stream, or have status report contentHead alongside headSequence so freshness comparisons are made against real activity.","severity":"low"}],"gateId":"judge-usefulness","nodeId":"judge","passed":false},"type":"gate_verdict"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-19T01:37:27.597969400Z","previousHash":"sha256:239690ca4129ca12c240967f4252267ccce70e11e92a44b6940fcb7cd186d8d7","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge9","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":19,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge9"}],"evidenceIds":["exec-exec-m08-judge9-judge-a1-judgment"],"expectedNextSequence":18,"formatVersion":"1.0.0","requestDigest":"sha256:9f2f31951bb381657389b348ff04ea32f72704d76ba2856e3baa6f4fc1135c42","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge9","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"streamId":"exec-m08-judge9"}
